---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Rabbit Holes" description="Deep-dive methodologies that power my work">
  <section class="hero-small">
    <h1>Rabbit <span class="highlight">Holes</span></h1>
    <p>The methodologies behind the work. Deep dives into how I solve problems.</p>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section intro-section">
    <p class="intro-text">
      Every project I build follows a methodology that's been refined across dozens of engagements. 
      These rabbit holes show you <strong>how</strong> I work — not just what I've built.
    </p>
    <p class="intro-sub">
      Each one connects to a core tenet and contains multiple projects as proof.
    </p>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <div class="rabbit-grid">
      
      <!-- Signal from Noise (Clarity Tenet) -->
      <article class="rabbit-card featured">
        <div class="rabbit-header">
          <div class="rabbit-status">
            <span class="status-dot active"></span>
            <span>Active Research</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/clarity/" class="tenet-badge">Clarity Tenet →</a>
        </div>
        <h2>Signal from Noise</h2>
        <p class="rabbit-subtitle">Turning overwhelming sources into accessible, actionable insight</p>
        <p class="rabbit-description">
          75,000 books. Hours of podcasts. Scattered content everywhere. The methodology: 
          systematic curation, AI enrichment, and progressive disclosure. The result: 
          people actually find what they need.
        </p>
        <div class="rabbit-projects">
          <span class="projects-label">Projects inside:</span>
          <div class="project-chips">
            <span class="chip">Freed Reads</span>
            <span class="chip">Investing Dojo</span>
            <span class="chip">Club Dadvice</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rabbit-meta">
          <span>Addresses: "We're drowning in content"</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/rabbit-holes/signal-from-noise/" class="rabbit-link">Explore the methodology →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Kitchen Confidence (Clarity + Insight Tenets) -->
      <article class="rabbit-card featured">
        <div class="rabbit-header">
          <div class="rabbit-status">
            <span class="status-dot active"></span>
            <span>Active Research</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/clarity/" class="tenet-badge">Clarity Tenet →</a>
        </div>
        <h2>Kitchen Confidence</h2>
        <p class="rabbit-subtitle">Making cooking fun and accessible through community, AI, and open data</p>
        <p class="rabbit-description">
          Cooking classes cost £100+. YouTube doesn't answer back. The methodology: 
          community-as-teacher, AI ingredient matching, and nostalgia-driven engagement. 
          Includes working video content.
        </p>
        <div class="rabbit-projects">
          <span class="projects-label">Projects inside:</span>
          <div class="project-chips">
            <span class="chip">Cookalong Platform</span>
            <span class="chip">Breaditation</span>
            <span class="chip">Aldi Spoof Ad</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rabbit-meta">
          <span>Addresses: "I'm intimidated in my own kitchen"</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/rabbit-holes/kitchen-confidence/" class="rabbit-link">Explore the methodology →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Storyselling (Story + Clarity Tenets) -->
      <article class="rabbit-card featured">
        <div class="rabbit-header">
          <div class="rabbit-status">
            <span class="status-dot active"></span>
            <span>Active Research</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/story/" class="tenet-badge">Story Tenet →</a>
        </div>
        <h2>Storyselling</h2>
        <p class="rabbit-subtitle">Creating solution stories that unite clients and colleagues</p>
        <p class="rabbit-description">
          Every business exists to solve a problem. This 5-phase methodology turns that 
          insight into a narrative that galvanises your entire community — internal and external.
        </p>
        <div class="rabbit-projects">
          <span class="projects-label">Frameworks inside:</span>
          <div class="project-chips">
            <span class="chip">Solution Stack</span>
            <span class="chip">One Newsletter</span>
            <span class="chip">TED Talk Script</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rabbit-meta">
          <span>Addresses: "Our message doesn't resonate"</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/rabbit-holes/storyselling/" class="rabbit-link">Explore the methodology →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- STAR Framework (Story + Insight Tenets) -->
      <article class="rabbit-card featured">
        <div class="rabbit-header">
          <div class="rabbit-status">
            <span class="status-dot active"></span>
            <span>Active Research</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/insight/" class="tenet-badge">Insight Tenet →</a>
        </div>
        <h2>The STAR Framework</h2>
        <p class="rabbit-subtitle">Cosmic storytelling principles that bypass cynicism through awe</p>
        <p class="rabbit-description">
          Synthesized from Carl Sagan's Cosmos: Shift perspective, articulate Tension, 
          introduce Awe, show Resolution. The methodology for breaking through when logic isn't working.
        </p>
        <div class="rabbit-projects">
          <span class="projects-label">Principles inside:</span>
          <div class="project-chips">
            <span class="chip">Cosmic Zoom</span>
            <span class="chip">Awe Before Argument</span>
            <span class="chip">Star-Stuff Identity</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rabbit-meta">
          <span>Addresses: "We can't get through the cynicism"</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/rabbit-holes/storytelling-frameworks/" class="rabbit-link">Explore the methodology →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- Building Intelligence (AI + Insight Tenet) -->
      <article class="rabbit-card featured">
        <div class="rabbit-header">
          <div class="rabbit-status">
            <span class="status-dot active"></span>
            <span>Active Research</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/insight/" class="tenet-badge">Insight Tenet →</a>
        </div>
        <h2>Building Intelligence</h2>
        <p class="rabbit-subtitle">Creating a "Room 40" system that turns data into action</p>
        <p class="rabbit-description">
          Most companies are drowning in reports but starving for wisdom. The methodology: 
          Cognitive diversity, the "Human Google" index, and the courage to interpret raw data.
        </p>
        <div class="rabbit-projects">
          <span class="projects-label">Principles inside:</span>
          <div class="project-chips">
            <span class="chip">The Human Index</span>
            <span class="chip">Context Engineering</span>
            <span class="chip">The Zimmerman Signal</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rabbit-meta">
          <span>Addresses: "We have data but no insight"</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/rabbit-holes/building-intelligence/" class="rabbit-link">Explore the methodology →</a>
      </article>
      
      <!-- The Insight Layer (Insight Tenet) - Coming Soon -->
      <article class="rabbit-card coming-soon">
        <div class="rabbit-header">
          <div class="rabbit-status">
            <span class="status-dot"></span>
            <span>Coming Soon</span>
          </div>
          <a href="/insight/" class="tenet-badge">Insight Tenet →</a>
        </div>
        <h2>The Insight Layer</h2>
        <p class="rabbit-subtitle">Synthesizing across sources to surface what matters</p>
        <p class="rabbit-description">
          You're data-rich and insight-poor. Multiple dashboards, no clarity. 
          The methodology for finding patterns that inform decisions.
        </p>
        <div class="rabbit-projects">
          <span class="projects-label">Will include:</span>
          <div class="project-chips">
            <span class="chip muted">Zeitgeist</span>
            <span class="chip muted">The Stack</span>
            <span class="chip muted">Research Synthesis</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      
    </div>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section cta-section">
    <h2>Want to go deeper on a methodology?</h2>
    <p>I'm always refining how I work. Let's talk about your problem.</p>
    <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com" class="cta-button">Start a Conversation</a>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero-small {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  
  .hero-small h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .hero-small p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  
  .intro-section {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  
  .intro-text {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #ccc;
    max-width: 700px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .intro-sub {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  
  .rabbit-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  
  .rabbit-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--border);
    position: relative;
  }
  
  .rabbit-card.featured {
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }
  
  .rabbit-card.coming-soon {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  
  .rabbit-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .rabbit-status {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  
  .status-dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--muted);
  }
  
  .status-dot.active {
    background: #22c55e;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.5);
  }
  
  .tenet-badge {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  
  .rabbit-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .rabbit-subtitle {
    color: #ccc;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  
  .rabbit-description {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .rabbit-projects {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .projects-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .project-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  
  .chip {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  
  .chip.muted {
    background: #1a1a1a;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  
  .rabbit-meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .rabbit-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  
  .rabbit-link:hover {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }
  
  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .cta-section p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
